James inquired about sharing a new National Geographic documentary from Disney+ with his students, noting its absence in his institution's library. I provided guidance on several approaches to address this challenge: 1) Reach out for a licensing option through the library, 2) Explore educational discounts from Disney+, 3) Arrange a classroom viewing either in-person or via video conferencing, 4) Encourage students to access it through personal subscriptions or trials, 5) Seek institutional support for platform subscriptions, and 6) Consider using supplemental materials related to the documentary. I emphasized the importance of complying with copyright laws and institutional policies while fostering ethical access to educational content.

